		2827 -> 2838;
	2828 [label="I... know what that's like. Before I started \"looping,\" I hurt myself pretty badly in Duviri. It healed, but it still aches something awful from time to time. I try to hide my wincing when it acts up.",shape=box,color=red];
		2828 -> 2839;
	2829 [label="Old persistent problems can sometimes be as problematic as new ones. Just because they come and go, and can stay with us, doesn't mean they aren't worth talking about.",shape=box,color=red];
		2829 -> 2840;
	2830 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	2834 [label="The mind is a truly marvelous thing. I think it is fascinating that they must always hurt, all the time, and yet I have learned to simply ignore them.",shape=box,color=blue];
		2834 -> 2835;
		2834 -> 2836;
		2834 -> 2837;
	2835 [label="I'm the same way. The moment I focus on - yeah, there's the pain. Sometimes I wonder if that's why I keep so damn busy.",shape=box,color=red];
		2835 -> 2845;
	2836 [label="Sometimes I get angry thinking about how much I could get done if I wasn't distracted by the pain all the time.",shape=box,color=red];
		2836 -> 2846;
	2837 [label="Are you always tired all the time, too? Sometimes I wonder if that's why I'm so exhausted. I'm always spending cycles on being in pain in the background.",shape=box,color=red];
		2837 -> 2847;
